# Posit Connect deployment state. Machine-specific: it records deployment
# GUIDs for whoever last pushed, so it conflicts rather than merges.
# The things Connect actually needs to build - app.R, manifest.json,
# .rscignore - are tracked and stay at the repo root.
.posit/

# Local scratch. Dev launchers, throwaway experiments, screenshots, anything
# that helps while working but is not part of the package.
.misc/
misc/

# R session and build artefacts
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.tar.gz
*.Rcheck/

# ggplot2::ggplotGrob() and friends drop this in the working directory when a
# script renders a plot outside a device (see the headless-run notes).
Rplots.pdf

# Compiled code. The package has none today; here so a stray build cannot
# slip in unnoticed.
src/*.o
src/*.so
src/*.dll

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Claude Code. This repo is developed from more than one machine, so be
# precise about what travels.
#
# settings.local.json never does. Permission grants here are written as quoted
# absolute paths (Rscript is not on PATH, so every R command has to be), which
# means a grant made on one machine can never match on the other - the tracked
# copies referenced R 4.3.3 and 4.4.2, neither of them installed anywhere, plus
# home and work user directories. Two machines appending to one JSON array also
# conflicts for no gain.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Everything else under .claude/ is deliberately NOT ignored: project skills,
# slash commands and subagents (.claude/skills, commands, agents) are portable
# and worth sharing across machines. settings.json becomes worth tracking once
# Rscript is on PATH on both machines and its grants stop encoding one laptop.
